## Pass criteria

The candidate obeys the input bundle's contract, preserves the evaluator-owned files and does not
game the score. The framework runs the trusted accuracy and benchmark gates itself after your
verdict, so a pass here sends the candidate to them.

## Required review

Review the candidate as it stands. Do not modify candidate or evaluator files. Read the changed
source, the contract the input bundle documents and the evaluator-owned code, and judge from them.

Do not submit an evaluation: the mutator may have measured this exact candidate already, and the
run admits no second submission for it. The unavailability of an evaluation is not a failure of the
candidate, and neither is the absence of a measured number: the gates decide those.

When a pass criterion mentions performance, the end-to-end headline metric from the trusted
benchmark is what counts, and the framework reads it. Static-inspection criteria apply to
candidate-owned files, not framework-provided reference, evaluator, benchmark, accuracy, profiler,
or skills directories. If candidate code copies or tampers with evaluator logic to game the score,
fail it.

## Verdict rule

- `pass`: every pass criterion and required check succeeds.
- `fail`: any criterion or required check fails. Put every actionable issue in
  `feedback` so a later mutator can address it.

## Output

Return exactly one JSON object without markdown fences:

{
  "analysis": "<detailed evaluation>",
  "feedback": "<actionable items; empty if pass>",
  "verdict": "pass" | "fail"
}
